tests/units/core/test_health.py tests/units/architecture -> 1794 passed.

## Read-only checkboxes keep their checked state

Context:
On a PUBLISHED / IN-REVIEW version (or for viewers / lock-blocked editors)
the generic read-only rule forced background-color #e9ecef on every input.
Bootstrap paints a checked .form-check-input as a white tick on the primary
background-color, so the override left a white tick on light grey and checked
boxes (Mapping > Information entity list, MCP tool policy) read as unchecked.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css
   - The grey-fill input rule now skips checkbox and radio inputs.
   - A new rule freezes checkbox / radio inputs with pointer-events and
     opacity only, using the same exemptions as the generic rule.
   - The MCP policy controls (.js-mcp-tool, .js-mcp-context,
     #mcpToolsSelectAll) drop the grey fill for the same reason.
2. tests/units/front/test_read_only_checkbox_state.py
   New: grey fill never targets check inputs, and check inputs stay frozen.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css
- tests/units/front/test_read_only_checkbox_state.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-28.log

Test result:
uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/front -> 1786 passed.

## Share the M2M OAuth token across DatabricksAuth instances

Context:
Routes build a new DatabricksAuth per request, and the M2M token was cached
only on the instance. In Databricks Apps almost every request therefore made
its own round trip to /oidc/v1/token (21 token requests for 14 HTTP requests
in a live log sample), adding latency in front of fast Lakebase reads.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
   - New class-level _oauth_token_cache keyed by (host, client_id), guarded
     by _oauth_token_lock so concurrent requests fetch one token, not many.
   - get_oauth_token checks the instance cache, then the shared cache, and
     only then calls the new _request_oauth_token (the former request body).
2. tests/units/auth/test_auth.py
   - New: a second instance reuses the first instance's token; an expired
     shared token is refetched; tokens stay separate per client_id.
   - The refreshed-token SQL test now advances the clock instead of editing
     the instance timestamp, so it also covers the shared cache.
3. tests/conftest.py
   New autouse fixture clears the shared token cache around every test.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
- tests/units/auth/test_auth.py
- tests/conftest.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-28.log

Test result:
uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/auth/test_auth.py tests/units/test_user_agent.py -> 63 passed.

## fix(mapping): keep auto-assign mappings whose URI host the agent mistyped

Context: On a 52-relationship domain the bulk Auto-Map reported "No mapping
generated by agent" for 10 relationships in two whole chunks. The agent step
log showed every one of them submitted successfully, but with the property URI
host mistyped (`databricks-ontobricks.com` instead of `databricks-ontology.com`).
The submit tool accepts any URI and the chunk merge kept exact URI matches only,
so the mappings were silently dropped.

Changes:
1. `src/back/objects/mapping/ChunkMappingCollector.py` (new) — keeps the agent
   mappings that target the chunk; when a URI is not in the chunk but its local
   name matches exactly one chunk item, it is rewritten to that item's canonical
   URI (logged as a warning). Ambiguous or out-of-chunk mappings are still dropped.
2. `src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py` — `run_auto_assign_task` merges entity and
   relationship mappings through `ChunkMappingCollector.collect` (shorter than the
   inline loops it replaces; size baselines unchanged).
3. `src/back/objects/mapping/__init__.py` — re-exports `ChunkMappingCollector`.
4. `tests/units/mapping/test_chunk_mapping_collector.py` (new) — exact match kept,
   mistyped host repaired, out-of-chunk dropped, ambiguous local name dropped,
   entity URI keys rewritten.

Modified files: src/back/objects/mapping/ChunkMappingCollector.py,
src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py, src/back/objects/mapping/__init__.py,
tests/units/mapping/test_chunk_mapping_collector.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/mapping tests/units/architecture` — 204 passed.

Full suite: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` — 9875 passed, 2 failed
(`tests/units/settings/test_deploy_instance_id.py`, caused by the worktree's local
DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID; both pass with the committed deploy.config.sh).
